  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Life-Saving Assistance to the Most Vulnerable Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) Affected by Crises Induced by Natural and Man-Made Hazards in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protracted and new displacements have continued to occur in Sudan due to decades of conflict and recurring disasters related to numerous natural hazards, mainly floods and droughts. Sudan is currently facing a myriad of challenges in managing responses to crises related to these human-induced and natural hazards, which have been exacerbated by a combination of political and socio-economic instability, placing affected populations under an extreme vulnerability. 
 
IOM is addressing critical humanitarian needs and contribute to building community resilience by providing emergency shelter (ES), non-food items (NFIs) and water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) to the most vulnerable crisis-affected populations in Sudan.</narrative>
  </description>
